  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Generator (no-pick 2D Chamfer).** The ride sectioned the model at Top of Part Z and put the cone tip on that outline at the corner depth. On a model whose edge already carries a modelled chamfer, that outline is the bevel's *top* edge, which sits inside the wall by the bevel's width. The cone then cut a V 0.71 mm into the part (QA p01-flange: `G1 X75 Y15.999 Z-3`, which is world y -14.001 against a wall at y -15), and the width moved only Z. Now `material_source` sections the source twice, at the top plane (the edges to break) and at the corner depth `top - width*tan(angle)` (the wall). The new `machining2d::chamfer_ride_loops` gives each top loop the wall loop within `width` of it. For a vertical wall the two loops are the same and the top loop itself is ridden, so sharp-edged parts post exactly as before. A top edge with no wall within the width (a blind pocket or island shallower than the chamfer depth) is refused by name, with the spot.\n\n**Verify (program sim).** The V passed because the op's edge-break record declared that same false edge, and any declared bevel got credit. A 2D Chamfer's records are now credited only where the cone tip stands on a wall: at every sample along the edge, the model's top 0.05 mm off the edge, on at least one side, must be no higher than the tip plus the verdict tolerance (`sim::stock_sim::on_walls`, new `wall_anchor.rs`). A record that fails is dropped and logged, and its columns are judged against the model, so the cut is a blocking gouge. Deburr records are not held to this: a deburr may legitimately break an obtuse 3D edge, such as a drafted wall. `program_breaks` moved from `stock_sim.rs` to `stock_sim_breaks.rs`, and `Planned` gained `walled`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/2435-chamfer-modelled-edge.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests, each mutation-checked:\n- `crates/app/tests/chamfer_modelled_edge.rs` (new). The model is a 40x20x10 brick with a modelled 1x45 chamfer on its top edges. It is the stock and the part, and one no-pick 2D Chamfer runs on it.\n  - `a_no_pick_chamfer_on_a_modelled_chamfer_rides_the_wall`: width 1. Every feed tip is at z 9 on the wall (x ±20 / y ±10), and the gate is clean.\n  - `the_width_moves_the_tip_along_the_bevel_not_only_in_z`: width 0.5. Tips are at z 9.5 on the bevel (±19.5 / ±9.5), and the gate is clean.\n  - `a_cone_tip_inside_the_part_is_a_gouge_not_edge_break_credit`: the old ride and its record are put back by hand, and the gate must report a gouge.\n- `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests` (4 unit tests: vertical wall unchanged, bevel rides the wall, too-far wall refuses, lower edge ignored).\n- `stock_sim::wall_anchor::tests` (2 unit tests: tip on the wall keeps its credit, tip inside loses it).\n\nMutations:\n- Generator fix reverted (ride the top section again): the two ride tests fail. With the fixed verify, the old ride is convicted end to end: `gouge ... 1175 cell(s), worst 0.94 mm`.\n- Wall filter disabled (`walled` ignored): the gouge test fails, because the gate passes the V.\n\nQA part (p01-flange, from the issue), run through `camcraft-cli process`:\n- No-pick width 1 now posts `X75 Y15 Z-3` (world y -15, z 14), with the gate ok.\n- Width 0.5 posts `Y15.5 Z-2.5`, with the gate ok.\n- The old ride, with this verify, is blocked: `gouge ... worst 1.00 mm` (w 1) and `worst 0.50 mm` (w 0.5).\n- The issue's picked-chain workaround project still posts, with the gate ok.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` : green, 215 steps, 0 failed (17.4 min), among them chamfer_modelled_edge, edge_break_gate, edge_break_bound, golden_cl, mill2d_b, setup_align_chamfer, setup_carry_credits, stock_chamfer_added_part, posting, solid_law_goldens, verify, and the motion and sim lib unit tests, plus `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The tilted (3+2) frame variant of the no-pick chamfer. The corner depth is taken in the frame's own Z, the same as the top plane, but no tilted test was added.\n- Curved bevels (a modelled round under a chamfer) beyond the QA STEP's R5 corners.\n- The UI. Pixel snapshots are untouched.\n- Windows/Linux.\n- The release-lane heavy suites.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer with no picked edges on a model whose edge is already chamfered now rides the wall under the bevel (the tip no longer cuts a V into the part), and verify now blocks a 2D Chamfer whose cone tip stands inside the part instead of crediting it as the edge break (#2435)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\nFork synced at: branched from upstream main abe24ff09\n\nFixes #2435\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
